## 7. Nginx Role

### Default variables

File: `roles/nginx/defaults/main.yml`

```yaml
---
nginx_package_name: nginx
nginx_service_name: nginx
nginx_service_enabled: true
```

### Role tasks

File: `roles/nginx/tasks/main.yml`

```yaml
---
- name: Install Nginx
  become: true
  ansible.builtin.apt:
    name: "{{ nginx_package_name }}"
    state: present
    update_cache: true

- name: Ensure Nginx is running and enabled
  become: true
  ansible.builtin.service:
    name: "{{ nginx_service_name }}"
    state: started
    enabled: "{{ nginx_service_enabled }}"

- name: Deploy Nginx configuration
  become: true
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    src: default
    dest: /etc/nginx/sites-available/default
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: '0644'
  notify: Reload Nginx
```

### Handler

File: `roles/nginx/handlers/main.yml`

```yaml
---
- name: Reload Nginx
  become: true
  ansible.builtin.service:
    name: nginx
    state: reloaded
```

## 8. Main Integrated Playbook

File: `playbooks/site.yml`

```yaml
---
- name: Automated Linux Server Configuration
  hosts: all
  become: true
  gather_facts: true

  tasks:
    - name: Display target server information
      debug:
        msg: "Configuring {{ inventory_hostname }}"

    - name: Install required packages
      ansible.builtin.apt:
        name:
          - nginx
          - busybox
          - ufw
        state: present
        update_cache: true

    - name: Create the DevOps group
      ansible.builtin.group:
        name: devops
        state: present

    - name: Create a user
      ansible.builtin.user:
        name: devopsuser
        group: devops
        state: present
        create_home: true
        shell: /bin/bash

    - name: Create application directory
      ansible.builtin.file:
        path: /opt/devops
        state: directory
        owner: devopsuser
        group: devops
        mode: '0755'

    - name: Create application log file
      ansible.builtin.copy:
        content: ""
        dest: /opt/devops/app.log
        owner: devopsuser
        group: devops
        mode: '0644'

    - name: Deploy environment-specific application configuration
      ansible.builtin.template:
        src: ../templates/app.conf.j2
        dest: /opt/devops/app.conf
        owner: devopsuser
        group: devops
        mode: '0644'

    - name: Configure Nginx using reusable role
      ansible.builtin.include_role:
        name: nginx

    - name: Allow SSH connection
      community.general.ufw:
        rule: allow
        port: '22'
        proto: tcp

    - name: Allow HTTP connection
      community.general.ufw:
        rule: allow
        port: '80'
        proto: tcp

    - name: Allow HTTPS connection
      community.general.ufw:
        rule: allow
        port: '443'
        proto: tcp

    - name: Set default incoming policy
      community.general.ufw:
        direction: incoming
        default: deny

    - name: Set default outgoing policy
      community.general.ufw:
        direction: outgoing
        default: allow

    - name: Enable UFW firewall
      community.general.ufw:
        state: enabled
```

**Note:** This is the submitted, tested playbook structure. Nginx is installed both in the package task and in the Nginx role; the separate package entry is redundant. The role already handles Nginx installation.

## 9. Deployment Commands

Run commands from the project root directory.

### Syntax validation

```bash
ansible-playbook --syntax-check playbooks/site.yml
```

### Deploy to Development

```bash
ansible-playbook -i inventory/dev playbooks/site.yml
```

### Deploy to Staging

```bash
ansible-playbook -i inventory/staging playbooks/site.yml
```

### Deploy to Production

```bash
ansible-playbook -i inventory/production playbooks/site.yml
```

